From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: hdmi-codec: allow odd PCM channel counts

The channel allocation lookup only matches allocations for exactly as
many channels as the stream has, and all of them are for 2, 4, 6 or 8
channels. A 3, 5 or 7 channel stream therefore fails hw_params with
"Not able to map channels to speakers", although the HDMI audio
InfoFrame takes any channel count from 2 to 8.

Match an odd count against the allocations for one channel more, in
the usual order. The speaker in the last slot stays silent.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c
@@ -370,7 +370,7 @@
 		/* If spk_alloc == 0, HDMI is unplugged return stereo config*/
 		if (!spk_alloc && cap->ca_id == 0)
 			return i;
-		if (cap->n_ch != channels)
+		if (cap->n_ch != round_up(channels, 2))
 			continue;
 		if (!(cap->mask == (spk_mask & cap->mask)))
 			continue;
